---
// LocalAI.astro — Unified local AI + privacy + BYO-AI section.
// Includes: on-device transcription flow diagram, all 6 AI providers,
// local model support, data residency, open-source transparency,
// offline capability, no telemetry, no accounts, Pro Mode text-only,
// no built-in/shared API key, Island behavioral properties,
// Deck behavioral properties. Green-tinted privacy band preserved.
---

<section class="section" id="privacy">
  <div class="container">

    <!-- ================================================================== -->
    <!-- 1. GREEN-TINTED PRIVACY BAND — "Private by architecture"           -->
    <!-- ================================================================== -->
    <div class="privacy-band reveal">
      <div class="privacy-grid">
        <!-- Left: claims -->
        <div>
          <span class="h-kicker shield-kicker">Private by architecture</span>
          <h2>Your voice stays local by default.</h2>
          <p class="section-lead">
            Local Transcription is the default. Cloud Transcription is available
            only when you deliberately select it and provide a provider key.
            Speech-to-text runs on your machine with
            <a href="https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--green);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px">faster-whisper</a>.
            Only finished text can ever reach a provider, and only
            if you opt in with your own key.
          </p>
          <ul class="privacy-points">
            <li>
              <svg class="ck" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-6"/>
              </svg>
              <span><b>Local mode keeps audio on-device.</b> Short dictation buffers are discarded after transcription; meeting recordings remain local until you delete them.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg class="ck" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-6"/>
              </svg>
              <span><b>Works fully offline</b> &mdash; turn Pro Mode off and nothing touches the network. Mumble keeps working with zero internet.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg class="ck" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-6"/>
              </svg>
              <span><b>No telemetry, no accounts</b> &mdash; Mumble doesn&rsquo;t phone home. No sign-up, no analytics, no usage tracking of any kind.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Right: the audio-vs-text flow diagram (preserved from existing) -->
        <div class="flowdiagram" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="fd-node audio">
            <div class="fd-ic">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="3" width="6" height="11" rx="3"/>
                <path d="M5 11a7 7 0 0014 0M12 18v3"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h4>Your audio</h4>
              <p>Recorded &amp; transcribed on-device with faster-whisper</p>
            </div>
            <span class="fd-stay">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <rect x="5" y="11" width="14" height="9" rx="2"/><path d="M8 11V8a4 4 0 018 0v3"/>
              </svg>
              Stays
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="fd-divider">
            <span>then, only if you opt in&hellip;</span>
            <span class="ln"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="fd-node text">
            <div class="fd-ic">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M5 5h14M5 10h14M5 15h9"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h4>Just the text</h4>
              <p>Sent to <em>your</em> AI, with <em>your</em> key</p>
            </div>
            <span class="fd-opt">Optional</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ================================================================== -->
    <!-- 2. PRO-MODE — text-only transmission (your own key)                 -->
    <!-- ================================================================== -->
    <div class="privacy-points" style="margin-top: 28px; max-width: 680px;">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p style="color:var(--text-dim);font-size:.96rem;line-height:1.65">
          <b style="color:var(--text)">Pro Mode itself sends text &mdash; not audio.</b>
          When you enable AI polish, only the transcribed text is sent for polish.
          The separate Cloud Transcription option sends audio only when you opt in.
          Every key you use is yours,
          stored only on your machine &mdash; you bring your own, or run a model
          entirely locally. Mumble never ships with a key, never bundles a
          default, and never supplies a key on your behalf.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ================================================================== -->
    <!-- 3. BRING YOUR OWN AI — provider logos + local model support         -->
    <!-- ================================================================== -->
    <div style="margin-top: clamp(50px, 7vw, 90px);" class="reveal">
      <span class="h-kicker">Your AI, your choice</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Bring your own AI keys.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead" style="margin-bottom: 40px;">
        Connect the provider you trust &mdash; or none at all.
        Mumble works with six AI back-ends, including running a model
        entirely on your own hardware.
      </p>

      <!-- Provider grid: 6 providers -->
      <div class="provider-grid">
        <!-- Cerebras -->
        <div class="provider">
          <svg class="pv-logo" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" fill="currentColor"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="pv-name">Cerebras</span>
          <span class="pv-tag">Fast inference</span>
        </div>

        <!-- OpenAI -->
        <div class="provider">
          <svg class="pv-logo" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M12 3l2 4 4 .6-3 3 .7 4-3.7-2-3.7 2 .7-4-3-3 4-.6 2-4z"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="pv-name">OpenAI</span>
          <span class="pv-tag">GPT models</span>
        </div>

        <!-- Anthropic -->
        <div class="provider">
          <svg class="pv-logo" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="16" rx="3"/>
            <path d="M12 8v8M8 12h8"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="pv-name">Anthropic</span>
          <span class="pv-tag">Claude models</span>
        </div>

        <!-- DeepSeek -->
        <div class="provider">
          <svg class="pv-logo" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M2 12h4l2-6 4 12 3-6h7"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="pv-name">DeepSeek</span>
          <span class="pv-tag">Reasoning</span>
        </div>

        <!-- Groq -->
        <div class="provider">
          <svg class="pv-logo" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M13 2L3 14h9l-1 8 10-12h-9l1-8z"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="pv-name">Groq</span>
          <span class="pv-tag">LPU speed</span>
        </div>

        <!-- Local (on-device) — gold accent -->
        <div class="provider local">
          <svg class="pv-logo" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="14" rx="2"/>
            <path d="M3 8h18M7 21h10"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="pv-name">Local</span>
          <span class="pv-tag">On your machine</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sub-points below the provider grid -->
      <ul class="byoai-features">
        <li>
          <svg class="ck" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-6"/>
          </svg>
          <span><b>20 one-tap AI presets</b> &mdash; 17 built-in (Summarise, Reply, Improve, Make formal, Extract action items, and more) plus 3 custom slots you define yourself.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg class="ck" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-6"/>
          </svg>
          <span><b>Your keys, and only yours</b> &mdash; every key is yours. Mumble never ships with a key, never bundles a default, and never supplies one on your behalf. No lock-in, no middleman.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg class="ck" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-6"/>
          </svg>
          <span><b>Run models locally</b> &mdash; connect a local model and keep everything &mdash; transcription, AI polish, and all data &mdash; on your own hardware.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg class="ck" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-6"/>
          </svg>
          <span><b>Open source</b> &mdash; released under the MIT License and built on 22 open-source libraries. The code is yours to inspect, fork, and trust.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- ================================================================== -->
    <!-- 4. ISLAND & DECK — behavioral properties                             -->
    <!-- ================================================================== -->
    <div style="margin-top: clamp(50px, 7vw, 90px);" class="reveal">
      <span class="h-kicker">Built to stay out of your way</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Island and Deck — floating tools that never steal focus</h2>
      <p class="section-lead" style="margin-bottom: 36px;">
        These aren&rsquo;t ordinary windows. They&rsquo;re designed
        to float above your work without interrupting it.
      </p>

      <div class="grid" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px;">
        <!-- Island card -->
        <article class="card sheen lift pad">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:14px;">
            <div style="width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:12px;display:grid;place-items:center;background:linear-gradient(160deg,rgba(212,175,55,.16),rgba(212,175,55,.04));border:1px solid rgba(212,175,55,.24);color:var(--gold);flex-shrink:0;">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22">
                <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="5"/>
                <path d="M8 12h8"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin:0;">The Island</h3>
          </div>
          <p style="color:var(--text-dim);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:16px;">
            A small floating pill that appears while you dictate. It sits above
            every other window and is <b style="color:var(--text)">click-through</b>
            &mdash; you can click right through it to the app behind.
            <b style="color:var(--text)">Always on top</b>, it never steals focus
            from what you&rsquo;re working on. It changes colour and label to
            show what&rsquo;s happening: Listening, Transcribing, the current mode,
            or Pasted.
          </p>
          <div class="chip-row">
            <span class="chip-sm">Click-through</span>
            <span class="chip-sm">Always on top</span>
            <span class="chip-sm gold">Never steals focus</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Deck card -->
        <article class="card sheen lift pad">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:14px;">
            <div style="width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:12px;display:grid;place-items:center;background:linear-gradient(160deg,rgba(212,175,55,.16),rgba(212,175,55,.04));border:1px solid rgba(212,175,55,.24);color:var(--gold);flex-shrink:0;">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22">
                <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="5" rx="1.5"/>
                <rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="5" rx="1.5"/>
                <path d="M6 18.5h12"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin:0;">The Deck</h3>
          </div>
          <p style="color:var(--text-dim);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:16px;">
            The Deck is your command centre: every transcript, clipboard item,
            and saved prompt in one searchable place. It is <b style="color:var(--text)">pinned by default</b>,
            floating on top of other windows. While pinned it becomes
            <b style="color:var(--text)">non-activating</b> &mdash; clicking it
            never steals focus, so whatever you have highlighted in another app
            stays live. Press <b style="color:var(--text)">Capture</b> in the Deck
            header to pull that highlighted text straight into the Deck as a new item.
          </p>
          <div class="chip-row">
            <span class="chip-sm">Pinned by default</span>
            <span class="chip-sm">Non-activating</span>
            <span class="chip-sm gold">Capture highlighted text</span>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ================================================================== -->
    <!-- 5. DATA RESIDENCY + TRUST FOOTER                                     -->
    <!-- ================================================================== -->
    <div style="margin-top: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px); text-align: center;" class="reveal">
      <div class="card pad" style="border-color: rgba(90,184,90,.22); background: radial-gradient(ellipse 50% 60% at 50% 10%, rgba(90,184,90,.04), transparent 60%), var(--glass-grad);">
        <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 32px;justify-content:center;align-items:center;font-size:.9rem;color:var(--text-dim);">
          <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--green)" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="18">
              <path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 4.5-3 7.6-7 9-4-1.4-7-4.5-7-9V6l7-3z"/>
              <path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/>
            </svg>
            Everything stored locally in <code style="font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--gold);font-size:.84rem;">%APPDATA%\Mumble</code>
          </span>
          <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--green)" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="18">
              <path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 4.5-3 7.6-7 9-4-1.4-7-4.5-7-9V6l7-3z"/>
              <path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/>
            </svg>
            No telemetry, no accounts, no sign-up
          </span>
          <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--green)" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="18">
              <path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 4.5-3 7.6-7 9-4-1.4-7-4.5-7-9V6l7-3z"/>
              <path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/>
            </svg>
            MIT Licensed &mdash; built on 22 open-source libraries
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
